::ingredients

(flour) 2 1/2 cups
(powdered sugar) 1/4 cup
(butter) 200g / 7oz
(sour cream, 18%) 1tbsp
(egg: yolk) 2
(salt) 1 pinch
(topping, your choice)
(walnuts, optional)
(pecans, optional)
(raisins, optional)
(almonds, sliced, optional)

::equipment

(baking sheet, large, 25x35cm / 10x14in)
(bowl)
(knife, sharp)
(plastic wrap)
(fridge)
(parchment paper)
(fork)

::instructions

{flour mixture} = (flour) + (butter)
    <place, in (bowl)>
(butter) <cut, into tiny pieces, using (knife)>
Meanwhile [
    {flour mixture} <mix>
]
{dough} = {flour mixture} + (egg: yolk) + (powdered sugar) + (sour cream) + (salt)
    <knead, well>
    <shape, into a ball>
    <wrap, in (plastic wrap)>
    <chill, in (fridge), ~1h>
    <roll, flat>
(baking sheet) <line, with (parchment paper)>
{dough} <place, on (baking sheet)>
    <prick, small holes, using (fork)>
    <bake, 200°C / 395°F, 15-20m>
    <cool>
(topping) <spread, on the cooled cake>
Optional [
    {dough} + (walnuts)
]
Optional [
    {dough} + (pecans)
]
Optional [
    {dough} + (raisins)
]
Optional [
    {dough} + (almonds)
]

::notes

For example, use orange jam made from 4 oranges as the topping. Decorate with nuts or other toppings of your choice.

::story

Mazurek is a traditional Polish flat cake made in many homes for Easter. Many different toppings are possible.


